Let me be concrete and accurate about WorkArena++ from my knowledge (flagged as background knowledge, not workspace-verified):
- WorkArena++ (Drouin et al., 2024) — a benchmark for LLM agents in realistic web-based office workflows (Gauzy project management tool). It has ~534 tasks across 7 domains (project management, finance, HR, etc.), each defined as a natural language instruction plus a set of API-based state checks (a "state check" / ground-truth JSON assertion over the app's database). Success = passing all checks. It uses an OpenAI-compatible API agent interface. Tasks have difficulty levels (easy/medium/hard). There's an agent scaffold (the "WorkArena++" agent) that uses a tool-calling loop with the app's REST API.
- The metric is success rate (fraction of tasks fully solved). Also there's a partial-credit / execution-based metric in some versions.

CoT prompting: The agent's system prompt / reasoning. The experiment manipulates whether the agent is instructed to produce chain-of-thought reasoning before acting (vs. direct/standard prompt).

Now, an important nuance: modern agents (GPT-4) use function calling; CoT is often implicitly done in the content before the tool call. So defining the IV precisely matters.

Design:
